# Diamond QC v3

Before major PR or production deploy, run the checklist in [`docs/protocol/diamond-qc-v3.md`](../../docs/protocol/diamond-qc-v3.md). Constitution: [`diamond-protocol-v1.md`](../../docs/protocol/diamond-protocol-v1.md) (living, opt-in).

**Do not develop during QC.** Measure → evidence → conclusion → minimal fix only.

**Axioms:** HTTP 200 ≠ content · Build PASS ≠ domain model · certainty ends at **measurement**.

**Production:** split **Availability** (HTTP) vs **Identity** (metadata / ORIGIN vs SCENARIO).

Identity layers (verify independently): **ORIGIN** · **SCENARIO** · **LOCATION** · **FIXTURES**.

**Domain Identity Leak** = *Scenario leaked into product identity* — scenario in global product metadata; semantic error, severity often **Medium**. (Mokotów / heat in title = example instance only.)

**Report:** business goal first → STATUS (fact vs forecast labels) → … → **RELEASE DECISION** (GO/NO-GO) → one next step.

**Hierarchy:** filary (public) → klucze interpretacyjne → protokoły — [`filary-i-klucze.md`](../../docs/protocol/filary-i-klucze.md).
